                <h2>Account Structure: Split by Channel First</h2>
<p>Before allocating budget, establish a clear account hierarchy:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Recommended account structure:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Meta Ads Manager</strong>: One campaign per objective (Traffic, Conversion, Retargeting)</li>
<li><strong>Google Ads</strong>: Separate campaigns for Search, Shopping, and Discovery</li>
<li><strong>TikTok</strong>: Separate ad account to avoid cross-channel interference</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<p>Each campaign should contain 2-3 ad sets covering different audiences or placements.</p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Common mistake to avoid:</strong><br />
Don't pile 80% of your budget into a single Meta campaign. One tool app discovered that splitting budgets across independent campaigns allowed algorithms to optimize faster, reducing CPA by 34% within 3 weeks.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Testing Phase Budget Allocation (Weeks 0-2)</h2>
<p>The testing phase focuses on validating creative and audience combinations—no scaling yet.</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Channel</th>
<th>Budget Allocation</th>
<th>Daily Budget per Ad Set</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Meta Traffic/Conversion</td>
<td>40%</td>
<td>$20-30</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Google Search/Shopping</td>
<td>25%</td>
<td>$15-25</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>TikTok</td>
<td>20%</td>
<td>$15-20</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Retargeting</td>
<td>15%</td>
<td>$10-15</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><strong>Execution steps:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Upload 3-5 creative sets per ad set—never judge with single creative</li>
<li>Test audience layers: Interest + Lookalike + Retargeting each in separate sets</li>
<li>Enable Meta CBO (Campaign Budget Optimization) to let algorithms distribute budget</li>
<li>Log CPA, CVR, and ROAS data daily</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Decision criteria:</strong> After testing, keep ad sets with CPA within 1.2x of target. Pause the bottom 50% performers.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Scaling Phase Budget Allocation (Weeks 3-6)</h2>
<p>Once data validates your approach, shift to scaling with performance-based budget distribution.</p>
<p><strong>Budget allocation priority:</strong></p>
<pre><code>ROAS ≥ 150% of target → Increase budget by 50-100%
ROAS 100-150% → Maintain and monitor
ROAS 70-100% → Reduce budget by 30%
ROAS &lt; 70% → Pause for optimization or terminate
</code></pre>
<p><strong>Scaling cadence:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Never increase daily budget by more than 20% at once (prevents platform risk triggers)</li>
<li>Maintain ratio: 60% running creatives + 40% new test creatives</li>
<li>Weekly review and reallocation of budget proportions</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Daily Monitoring &amp; Dynamic Adjustments</h2>
<p>Budget allocation is not a one-time task—it requires continuous iteration.</p>
<p><strong>Daily KPIs to monitor:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Actual spend vs. planned spend by channel (investigate if deviation exceeds 15%)</li>
<li>CPA fluctuations per ad set (analyze causes for changes over 20%)</li>
<li>Account balance alerts (recharge when balance drops below 1.5x weekly budget)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Weekly optimization checklist:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Export ad reports, sort by ROAS</li>
<li>Aggregate spend and conversion data by channel</li>
<li>Reallocate budget proportions for next week</li>
<li>Pause ad sets with zero conversions for 7+ consecutive days while spending over $50</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Key Reminders</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Don't scale all channels simultaneously</strong>: Stabilize 1-2 main channels first before expanding</li>
<li><strong>Don't skip testing budget</strong>: Skimping on testing may cost 5x more in scaling waste</li>
<li><strong>Plan recharges in advance</strong>: Avoid balance depletion causing ad interruptions that destabilize algorithms</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Quick Execution Checklist</h2>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Account structure split by channel complete</li>
<li>[ ] Testing phase budget ratios set</li>
<li>[ ] Minimum $15 daily budget per ad set confirmed</li>
<li>[ ] Daily data logging established</li>
<li>[ ] Recharge scheduled before balance drops below 1.5x weekly budget</li>
<li>[ ] Weekly budget reallocation completed</li>
</ul>
<p>Following this SOP, account budget structures typically become clear within 4-6 weeks, with a realistic expectation of 20-40% ROI improvement.</p>
